I don't think this impacts users, the settings are still registered properly and available in the editor. The only difference is that if the theora module is disabled at compile, then those settings aren't exposed anymore.

Which IMO makes sense because they're a no-op in this case. One potential drawback if people go back and forth between theora-enabled and disabled build is that they could lose some config, but that doesn't seem like a likely scenario.

